    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (76.43), whose elite sprint speed and favorable matchup against P. Lambert make him our premier offensive engine. With a significant boost from a dynamic platoon advantage and a leadoff spot, he is the clear centerpiece. **Colt Keith** (68.51) also profiles as a top-tier asset; his matchup against Young, combined with strong SP skill metrics and favorable park factors, provides an excellent efficiency floor. **Dillon Dingler** (63.89) remains a high-upside play at catcher, benefiting from a strong platoon advantage against Rogers and a premium spot in the order, which mitigates the risk posed by the opposing pitcher\u2019s respectable 3.97 xERA.\n\nTactical adjustments remain crucial as we navigate the scarcity of stolen bases. **Caleb Durbin** (56.30) and **Hyeseong Kim** (52.75) are rostered primarily for their speed, though their utility is slightly dampened by wind-in factors and elite pick-off/hold tendencies from their respective opposing pitchers. On the bench, **Casey Schmitt** (50.53) presented the most difficult decision; while his matchup against Schultz offered strong SP-based potential, his lower raw efficiency and a negative dynamic platoon split kept him out of the final lineup. We are also closely monitoring the lineup security for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** against Messick, as the opposing starter's 3.36 xERA presents a legitimate challenge that could suppress our overall run production. Caution is advised with **Junior Caminero**, whose score was dragged down by wind-in conditions at the park, making him a marginal start that we will monitor closely throughout the early innings.",
